{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.QResolvent","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.QResolvent","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Defs"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QResolventAlg.first_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QResolventAlg.first_identity","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-resolvent.lean#L84-L98","doc":"**First resolvent identity** (repaired form of the removed axiom).\nFor two resolvents of the same `Δ`:\n`R(s₁) − R(s₂) = (s₂ − s₁) R(s₁) R(s₂)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QResolventAlg.right_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QResolventAlg.right_inv","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-resolvent.lean#L82-L82","doc":"`R (s + Δ) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QResolventAlg.left_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QResolventAlg.left_inv","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-resolvent.lean#L80-L80","doc":"`(s + Δ) R = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QResolventAlg.R","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QResolventAlg.R","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-resolvent.lean#L78-L78","doc":"The resolvent `R_q(s)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QResolventAlg.s","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QResolventAlg.s","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-resolvent.lean#L76-L76","doc":"The spectral parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QResolventAlg.delta_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QResolventAlg.delta_q","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-resolvent.lean#L74-L74","doc":"The q-Laplacian `Δ̂_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QResolventAlg.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QResolventAlg.mk","kind":"ctor","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-resolvent.lean#L72-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QResolventAlg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QResolventAlg","kind":"structure","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-resolvent.lean#L66-L82","doc":"**q-Resolvent in an algebra (repaired form).**\n\n`A` is an algebra over a commutative ring `K` (in the paper, the\nconvolution algebra `𝓗_q` over the ground ring). The spectral parameter\nis a scalar `s : K`, and `R` is a two-sided inverse of `s + Δ`. Unlike\n`QResolvent`, this ties `R` to `s`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QResolvent.not_first_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QResolvent.not_first_identity","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-resolvent.lean#L48-L63","doc":"**The former axiom `QResolvent.first_identity` was false** (removed\n2026-11-15). It claimed the first resolvent identity\n  `∀ x, R₁.R x - R₂.R x = (R₂.s - R₁.s) * R₁.R (R₂.R x)`\nfor every pair of `QResolvent`s, but the structure only records\n`R ∘ delta_q = id`, which does not tie `R` to the spectral parameter `s`.\nOver `ℤ`, take `delta_q = R = id` with `s = 0` and `s = 1`: at `x = 1`\nthe identity reads `0 = 1`. A true identity needs the field\n`(s + delta_q) ∘ R = id` in an algebra; recorded as open in bean\n`qou-n2un`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QResolvent.inverse_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QResolvent.inverse_witness","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-resolvent.lean#L46-L46","doc":"Inverse witness: (s + delta_q) ∘ R = id and R ∘ (s + delta_q) = id.\nEncoded at the element level via a nominal multiplication. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QResolvent.R","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QResolvent.R","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-resolvent.lean#L43-L43","doc":"The resolvent R_q(s). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QResolvent.s","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QResolvent.s","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-resolvent.lean#L41-L41","doc":"The spectral parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QResolvent.delta_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QResolvent.delta_q","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-resolvent.lean#L39-L39","doc":"The q-Laplacian endomorphism. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QResolvent.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QResolvent.mk","kind":"ctor","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-resolvent.lean#L37-L37","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QResolvent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QResolvent","kind":"structure","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-resolvent.lean#L27-L46","doc":"**q-Resolvent data.**\n\nA categorical resolvent packages the q-Laplacian `delta_q`, the\nspectral parameter `s`, and an inverse witness for\n`s + delta_q` in the convolution algebra.\n\nThe field `inverse_witness` encodes that `(s + delta_q) * R = 1`\nin 𝓗_q; the resolvent identity R_q(s₁) - R_q(s₂) = (s₂-s₁) R_q(s₁) R_q(s₂)\nfollows from Hopf-algebra associativity. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:q-resolvent","label":"def:q-resolvent","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-resolvent.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}